Beryllium: online services off by default, no built-in services server

Purpose: charter decision D3 (owner, 1 November 2026) says Beryllium does
  not use Helium's online services. Building the feature matrix
  (4 November 2026) found the code did not do that: Helium registers
  helium.services.enabled as true (helium/core/services-prefs.patch) and
  falls back to https://services.helium.imput.net when no server is set
  (GetServicesBaseURL), held back only by helium.services.user_consented,
  which the setup page sets (helium/core/onboarding-page.patch). Accepting
  the setup page's defaults could therefore send extension, !bangs,
  filter-list, dictionary and component requests to Helium's server. The
  idle privacy test passed only because it starts with --no-first-run.
  This patch:
  - registers helium.services.enabled false, so a new profile has
    services off;
  - removes Helium's address as the built-in server (kHeliumDefaultOrigin
    is now empty): GetServicesBaseURL returns the unreachable dummy origin
    when no server is set, whichever caller asks, and ShouldAccessServices
    also requires a server, so turning services on without one does
    nothing;
  - changes the Settings text for the server field to say that none is
    built in, shows an example address instead of Helium's, and accepts
    http://localhost, 127.0.0.1 and [::1] as well as HTTPS, for a test
    server on the same machine (the C++ check already allowed these).
  Using Helium's servers stays possible as an explicit choice: turn
  services on in Settings and enter https://services.helium.imput.net as
  the server. When Beryllium hosts its own instance, its origin goes in
  kHeliumDefaultOrigin and everything else here stays.
  Existing profiles: one that never changed the services switch now has
  services off; one that turned it on explicitly keeps it on but has no
  server until one is entered.
Stage: 4 (Beryllium series). Depends on helium/core/services-prefs.patch
  and helium/core/onboarding-page.patch (stage 3), and on Helium's
  ublock-helium-services, component-updates, add-updater-preference,
  proxy-extension-downloads, reenable-spellcheck-downloads and
  add-native-bangs patches, which all reach the services through
  ShouldAccessServices and GetServicesBaseURL.
Refreshed against: Chromium 156.0.8078.79, Helium 0.20.3 (2f81b9ca),
  FreeBSD ports 6ad3e0c8, using freebsd/tools/patch-workbench; the new
  input pattern checked in JavaScript's v-flag mode, as the browser
  compiles it.
Test: freebsd/tests/browser/tests/test_60_privacy.py ServicesOff: services
  are off in a new profile, and with them switched on and consent given
  but no server set, an idle browser contacts no host. Feature matrix row
  P-SVC-01.
security-review: not required (removes network behaviour; the settings
  input still only reaches the existing origin validation)

--- a/components/helium_services/helium_services_helpers.h
+++ b/components/helium_services/helium_services_helpers.h
@@ -12,8 +12,10 @@
 
 namespace helium {
 
-const char kHeliumDefaultOrigin[] =
-    "https://services.helium.imput.net";
+// Beryllium: no services server is built in. Beryllium does not use
+// Helium's (services.helium.imput.net) unless the user enters it in
+// Settings; when Beryllium hosts its own instance, its origin goes here.
+const char kHeliumDefaultOrigin[] = "";
 
 const char kHeliumDummyOrigin[] =
     "https://helium-services-are-disabled.qjz9zk";
--- a/components/helium_services/helium_services_helpers.cc
+++ b/components/helium_services/helium_services_helpers.cc
@@ -70,7 +70,11 @@
         return *user_url;
     }
 
-    return GURL(kHeliumDefaultOrigin);
+    // Beryllium: with no server set and none built in (kHeliumDefaultOrigin
+    // is empty, so invalid), every services URL is the unreachable dummy,
+    // whichever caller asks.
+    GURL built_in(kHeliumDefaultOrigin);
+    return built_in.is_valid() ? built_in : GetDummyURL();
 }
 
 GURL GetDummyURL() {
@@ -78,8 +82,11 @@
 }
 
 bool ShouldAccessServices(const PrefService& prefs) {
+    // Beryllium: services also need a server, since none is built in.
     return prefs.GetBoolean(prefs::kHeliumServicesEnabled) &&
-           prefs.GetBoolean(prefs::kHeliumServicesConsented);
+           prefs.GetBoolean(prefs::kHeliumServicesConsented) &&
+           (GURL(kHeliumDefaultOrigin).is_valid() ||
+            GetValidUserOverridenURL(prefs).has_value());
 }
 
 bool ShouldAccessExtensionService(const PrefService& prefs) {
--- a/chrome/browser/ui/browser_ui_prefs.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ui/browser_ui_prefs.cc
@@ -261,7 +261,8 @@
   {
     registry->RegisterIntegerPref(prefs::kHeliumSchemaVersion, 0);
     registry->RegisterBooleanPref(prefs::kHeliumDisableSchemaAlerts, false);
-    registry->RegisterBooleanPref(prefs::kHeliumServicesEnabled, true);
+    // Beryllium: online services are off in a new profile (charter D3).
+    registry->RegisterBooleanPref(prefs::kHeliumServicesEnabled, false);
     registry->RegisterBooleanPref(prefs::kHeliumBangsEnabled, true);
     registry->RegisterBooleanPref(prefs::kHeliumExtProxyEnabled, true);
     registry->RegisterBooleanPref(prefs::kHeliumSpellcheckEnabled, true);
--- a/chrome/browser/resources/settings/privacy_page/services_page.html
+++ b/chrome/browser/resources/settings/privacy_page/services_page.html
@@ -142,9 +142,9 @@
     </div>
     <cr-input
         id="heliumOriginOverride"
-        placeholder="https://services.helium.imput.net"
+        placeholder="https://services.example.org"
         value="[[prefs.helium.services.origin_override.value]]"
-        pattern="https://.*"
+        pattern="https://.*|http://(localhost|127\.0\.0\.1|\[::1\])(:[0-9]+)?/?"
         on-keydown="onOriginOverrideKeydown_"
         on-change="onOriginOverrideChange_"
         type="url"
--- a/chrome/app/settings_strings.grdp
+++ b/chrome/app/settings_strings.grdp
@@ -1749,7 +1749,7 @@
       Use your own instance of Helium services
     </message>
     <message name="IDS_SETTINGS_HELIUM_SERVICES_OVERRIDE_DESCRIPTION" desc="Description of the text input for overriding the Helium services server">
